Just a few very minor optimisations, and a cleanup of the config and package generation.

`quantile` derives into `quantile_1`, because the compiler will see that at the moment of entering `quantile_1`, the inputs are already for sure an integer and a list, and therefore can skip verifying the type on each iteration. This doesn't happen to `quantile`, because it is a publicly exposed module and it can be called with whatever, hence each call needs to verify the type. Likewise when splitting `insert_tail` from `insert`.

